ollaborate closely with embedded software engineers to ensure seamless hardware/software integration</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Maintain and improve our component library and hardware development documentation</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Participate in hardware reviews and contribute to design decisions with a focus on robustness, manufacturability, and EMI mitigation</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Interface with manufacturing partners to support DFM (Design for Manufacturing) and bring designs into series production</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Passionate about drones, robotics, and innovative hardware systems</span></p></li></ul> <br> <ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering or a related field.</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">5+ years of hands-on experience in electronics development, especially in schematic capture and PCB layout (e.g., using Altium Designer or KiCad).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Solid understanding of analog and digital circuit design, power management, and embedded systems.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Working knowledge of EWIS (Electrical Wiring InterConnect System / Electrical Wiring InterConnection System</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Practical experience with radio/data link modules and wireless communication systems.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Basic experience in embedded programming (e.g., C or C++) is a plus.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Familiarity with lab equipment for hardware testing (oscilloscopes, multimeters).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A structured and pragmatic problem solver with a hands-on mindset.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Willingness to learn, take ownership, and grow within a collaborative engineering culture.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Eager to work closely with a multidisciplinary team of mechanical, software, and flight testing engineers.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Fluent in English, German is beneficial</span></p></li></ul><h3></h3><h3><strong><span style="color:#121317">Why TYTAN?</span></strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Build technology with real operational impact:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Develop autonomous defense systems designed to protect lives and strengthen Europe’s security.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Shape scalable defense capabilities:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Work on solutions built for mass deployment, cost efficiency, resilience, and reliable production at scale.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Contribute to networked air defense:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Help integrate our systems into multi-layered defense architectures alongside sensors, command systems, and effectors.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Develop for real-world operations:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Build capabilities together with end users and improve them continuously based on direct operational feedback.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Move fast and take ownership:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Work in a focused, high-performance team where decisions are made quickly and individual contributions have immediate impact.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Define a new generation of defense technology:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Join early and help shape the products, engineering standards, culture, and direction of a fast-growing deep-tech company.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Work with an international mission-driven team:</span></strong><span style="c