cial Sciences is an internationally active research institute and member of the Leibniz Association, funded by federal and state governments.</span><span style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;"><br> <br>Starting on<strong> 01.01.2027 </strong>our<strong> Department Data and Research on Society</strong>, <strong>Team Social Surveys</strong> located in <strong>Mannheim</strong>, is looking for a<br> <br><strong>Postdoctoral Researcher for Longitudinal Surveys (Salary group 13 TV-L, working time 100 %, Limitation for two years)</strong><br> <br></span><p style="line-height:115%;"><span style="line-height:115%;font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">Monitoring current social developments is a primary objective of the social sciences. The department </span><span style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;"><a href="https://www.gesis.org/en/institute/departments/data-and-research-on-society"><strong><span style="line-height:115%;color:rgb(0,112,192);">Data and Research on Society</span></strong></a></span><span style="line-height:115%;font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,112,192);font-size:15px;"> </span><span style="line-height:115%;font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">supports the social sciences in this task, by providing comprehensive data and tools to describe and analyse social changes. The department is responsible, among others for the implementation of the renowned European Social Survey (<a href="https://www.europeansocialsurvey.org/"><span style="color:#0070C0;"><strong>ESS</strong></span></a></span>) in Germany, and for the first time also for the collection of German data for the CROss-National Online Survey (<span style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;"><a href="https://www.europeansocialsurvey.org/methodology/methodological-research/modes-data-collection/cronos"><strong><span style="line-height:115%;color:rgb(0,112,192);">CRONOS</span></strong></a></span><span style="line-height:115%;font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">), implemented within the ESS framework. The CRONOS sample in Germany was recruited in the 12th ESS round, respondents will be invited to participate in at least two panel waves.</span></p></p><br><strong>Your tasks will be:</strong><p><ul style="list-style-type:disc;margin-left:15.05px;"><li style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">Planning and implementing CRONOS within the framework of the EU-funded INNOVATE Project initiated by ESS ERIC and further partners, in close cooperation with partners within and outside the institute </li><li style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">Planning and implementing the 13th round of the European Social Surveys (ESS) in Germany </li><li style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">Planning, coordinating and contributing to the German Translation of the ESS Source Questionnaire, and the fieldwork materials for the 13th round of ESS and for CRONOS</li><li style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">Checking and processing the data collected in the ESS and in CRONOS in Germany during and after the data collection</li><li style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">Presenting and publishing ESS-relevant research in scientific conferences and journals</li></ul></p><br><strong>Your profile:</strong><p><ul style="list-style-type:disc;margin-left:4.199999999999999px;"><li style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">Above-average completed PhD (as well as a Master) in the Social Sciences (for example Sociology, Political Science, Social Psychology, Survey Methodology)</li><li style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">Sound knowledge in empirical quantitative social research including the use of statistical analysis methods and programs (Stata, R)</li><li style="font-family:Tahoma, Geneva, sans-serif;font-si