a stewards and cross-functional governance teams.</li><li>Help clients establish practical approaches to <strong>data quality management</strong>, including quality rules, monitoring, issue resolution and accountability.</li><li>Shape <strong>metadata management practices</strong>, including business glossaries, data catalogs and data lineage, to improve transparency and a shared understanding of data.</li><li>Translate <strong>governance requirements into processes and tooling needs</strong>, working closely with business stakeholders and technical experts from our development department.</li><li>Prepare and facilitate workshops, develop training and communication materials, and support the <strong>adoption of governance practices</strong> across business and IT teams.</li><li>Connect governance initiatives to <strong>data products and AI use cases</strong>, define measures of success, and communicate recommendations through clear, management-ready deliverables.</li></ul><strong>Additional responsibilities as Senior Data Governance Consultant: <br></strong><ul><li><strong>Lead data governance projects or major workstreams end-to-end</strong>, taking responsibility for scope, approach, deliverables, quality and stakeholder alignment.</li><li>Act as a <strong>trusted advisor to senior client stakeholders</strong> on data governance, ownership and operating model decisions.</li><li>Guide clients through <strong>organizational change</strong>, resolve competing stakeholder priorities and ensure governance practices become part of day-to-day operations.</li><li>Further develop our <strong>data governance methods, frameworks and service offerings</strong>, and contribute to business development through proposals and client discussions.</li><li><strong>Mentor junior colleagues</strong> and promote knowledge sharing on data governance and data management.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Your profile</strong><p><ul><li>Degree<strong> in data science, artificial intelligence, stati