ferrer nofollow" href="https://wundergraph.com/blog/category/culture"><u>Building the Company We Always Wanted to Work In</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We invite everyone that wants to join us to understand our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/wundergraph/Mission-and-Core-Beliefs-20fb19e0a0ec80c09646fa9101368bce"><u>Core Beliefs </u></a>and  if you want to make an impact, have your voice heard, and work in a no-BS organization where you can get stuff done, look no further and apply today so we can chat.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ABOUT THE ROLE</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Product Designer at WunderGraph, you are the connection between what our users will find most helpful and what our engineers build. Considering the users also happen to be other developers, this becomes an interesting challenge to think about the Developer Experience as the User Experience. You combine sharp user insight, craft, and pragmatism to deliver experiences that are elegant, usable, and built to scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a wide-reaching role, as design roles at a startup should be. One week you might be running user interviews to shape a new feature; the next, refining our design system or designing a marketing landing page. You ground your work in evidence rather than assumption, partner closely with product and engineering, and turn what you learn about users into a clear, informed UX strategy that guides where we go next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>TEAM INTEGRATION</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reports to the VP of Product; is part of the Product team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aligns closely with the CEO (Product) and Head of Customer Success (customer experience and business impact)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate within the Product team with the Delivery Lead and the Design Engineer</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborates cross-functionally with engineering, marketing, product, and customer success</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ROLE OBJECTIVES</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are successful if you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of the complete design lifecycle, bridging the gap between initial discovery and final delivery for web and product interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cultivate an evidence-based UX strategy that leverages user research and data to steer the product's evolution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee the growth of a unified and extensible design system that spans both our product and marketing efforts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Convert user insights and organizational objectives into pragmatic, human-centric solutions engineered for long-term scalability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advocate for excellence in accessibility, responsiveness, and performance as fundamental pillars of your craft.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide mentorship to the team, sharing expertise in research methodologies and design principles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Refine the visual and functional identity of WunderGraph through meticulous and high-impact design work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact high-level product strategy by demonstrating how user-focused decisions drive tangible business impact.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ROLE TASKS</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role focuses on, but is not limited to:</p><h3><strong>Product Design</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and prototype user flows, interfaces, and interactions with scalability in mind.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own design problems end to end. From initial concept through execution and iteration after launch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rapidly produce wireframes, prototypes, and high-fidelity designs, exploring multiple concepts and iterating quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and evolve our design system and component library, keeping it consistent and maintainable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with engineers on feasibility, quality, and handoff, contributing to technical decisions (and coding where you're comfortable and it helps as a plus, not a requirement).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introduce advanced prototyping, interaction design, and motion practices.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>UX Research &amp; Strategy</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and conduct user research across discovery and validation via user interviews, surveys, usability testing, and competitor analysis.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn ambiguous product questions into decision-grade research that maps to real product and design decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Synthesize findings into clear insights, personas, journey maps, and opportunity areas that the team can act on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain a shared insight repository so learning is reusable, searchable, and available to everyone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate research into an informed, evolving UX strategy that guides the roadmap and anchors design direction in real user needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advocate for the user in prioritization and roadmap discussions, and define what "better" looks like through clear UX success metrics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run discovery workshops and share insights so research shows up where decisions are made like in  design reviews, product planning, and standups embedding user knowledge from the get-go.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Web &amp; Brand Experience</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the design and evolution of WunderGraph's web presence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver assets that span product and marketing: landing pages, visuals, campaign graphics, and interactive components.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape and maintain a cohesive style guide, balancing design innovation with consistency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support brand storytelling with motion graphics and interactive elements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ROLE REQUIREMENTS</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Senior-level experience in Product Design or UX/UI Design, with a strong portfolio of shipped work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience planning and running UX research (both generative and evaluative) and turning findings into strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in Figma, prototyping tools, and Adobe Creative Suite.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong background in UX and interaction design, accessibility, responsive design, and usability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience contributing to or leading design systems and component libraries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable using data and research to inform and defend design decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of front-end technologies (HTML/CSS, JavaScript a plus) enough to collaborate closely with engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication, storytelling, and collaboration skills in English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A self-starter who is comfortable with ambiguity and can lead initiatives independently in a fast-moving startup.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working 100% remotely in a distributed team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel occasionally for team retreats and workshops.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why WunderGraph?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work from wherever you thrive—we’re fully remote and globally distributed. If you're in Miami, come work with us in person! We also provide co-working space options worldwide if needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pick your preferred work hardware</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We focus on getting stuff done, and on having fun whilst doing so: work hard, play hard!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can make a real difference and find lots of opportunities to grow together with us</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discretionary PTO: take the time you need to recharge</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Depending on location, we offer healthcare benefits according to local standards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team retreats across the globe</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Note: This is a full-time, fully remote position, but we're prioritising candidates from EMEA. We are looking for someone who is available to work during European (CET) business hours.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Process</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We respect your time and interest in WunderGraph. This is why we're aiming to make the process as fast as possible. Here's what you can expect:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 min intro call with Mariya from our People team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">45 min discussion with the hiring manager. Following this, you might receive a small take home assignment related to the role. This is your chance to prove your skill!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complete the assignment and review together with hiring manager</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meet the founders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Culture fit call with team members</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our process also includes reference and background checks. We aim to respond or provide feedback in 2 or 3 days between each stage of the process. We're usually hiring through Deel as our Employer of Record, except for Germany or Florida where we're hiring directly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">WunderGraph is an equal opportunity workplace; we welcome people from all backgrounds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can find out more about our ways of working together here:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/wundergraph/WunderGraph-Public-Handbook-and-Resources-20db19e0a0ec800690cac27c35fadc73"><u>WunderGraph Public Handbook and Resources</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking forward to your application so we can grow together!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/wundergraph/senior-product-designer-emea-frankfurt-193620","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"EMEA","created_at":1791632412},{"slug":"chief-of-staff-berlin-296659","company_name":"Ceezer","title":"Chief of Staff (f/d/m)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">A definitive shift is currently happening. Corporates across the globe are no longer just reporting on sustainability; they are actively investing in it as a core financial and strategic asset.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At CEEZER, we are architecting the infrastructure for enterprise-grade Climate Performance Asset management, transforming how the world's largest companies source and manage carbon credits, Energy Attribution Certificates (EAC), and Sustainable Aviation Fuel certificates (SAFc).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>THE ROLE</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our platform gives the world’s most ambitious enterprises the data-driven precision, real-time monitoring, and framework-compliant reporting required to confidently deploy capital toward high-impact Climate Performance Asset portfolios and true, measurable climate action.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>YOUR MISSION</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Chief of Staff to work directly alongside our CEO; a sharp, structured operator who turns ambiguous, company-level problems into clear decisions and shipped outcomes, and who creates the clarity and cadence a fast-scaling team needs to execute.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner directly with the CEO to develop company strategy and translate it into clear priorities, and own the operating cadence that keeps the leadership team aligned and accountable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the highest-priority cross-functional initiatives end to end, from framing the problem to landing the outcome, especially where no single team owns them yet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structure ambiguous, company-level questions into sharp analysis and clear recommendations that shape executive and board decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own board meetings, investor updates, and leadership offsites, turning complex inputs into decision-ready materials.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the operating rhythms such as goal-setting, reporting, and business reviews that let a fast-scaling team execute without losing focus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted proxy for the CEO across internal and external meetings, representing their priorities and following through on decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support special projects across strategy, operations, and fundraising, contributing to business priorities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>WHAT YOU NEED TO SUCCEED</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years in top-tier management consulting, or a comparable strategy, investment, or high-growth startup background.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of owning ambiguous, cross-functional problems and driving them to a measurable outcome with limited direction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong structured problem-solving, with excellent Excel and PowerPoint skills and the ability to turn messy data into a clear recommendation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sharp written and verbal communication that earns trust with senior leaders, investors, and cross-functional teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort operating in a fast-moving environment, switching fluidly between high-level strategy and hands-on execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English is required; German is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A valid working permit in Germany.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>WHAT’S IN IT FOR YOU AT C</strong>EEZER?</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A mission that matters:</strong> Join a rapidly growing, dynamic team of international changemakers who are passionate about solving the world’s most pressing challenge and help shape a sustainable, net-zero future.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A learning culture</strong>: Take your skills to the next level with exciting growth opportunities, hands-on learning experiences, and access to resources designed to fuel your professional journey in a start-up that prioritizes learning and growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A diverse environment:</strong> Thrive in an inclusive environment where diversity is celebrated, and your unique perspective helps us flourish as a team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A net-zero career</strong>: From day one, your professional and personal carbon footprint is neutralized—because at CEEZER, sustainability isn’t just our mission, it’s how we operate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An attractive package</strong>: Enjoy perks like free Urban Sports Club membership, a discounted public transport, a company pension scheme, team events and offsites, and more…</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The hiring process</h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An intro call with the People Team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A call with our CEO, Magnus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A deep-dive case study.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Excited to create impact with us?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you don't meet every requirement but have <strong>exceptional strengths</strong> that could make you <strong>excel in this role</strong>, we'd love to hear from you. Apply now and let's discuss your potential.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We prohibit discrimination or harassment of any kind and make employment and other employee lifecycle decisions based solely on merit, skills, and potential. We actively work to recognize and address unconscious biases, fostering an environment where all individuals feel valued and empowered to succeed. We welcome <strong>diverse applicants</strong> and are dedicated to providing <strong>equal opportunities</strong> for everyone to thrive. Please let us know if you have any specific needs regarding this application process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About us</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">CEEZER is the leading partner for Climate Performance Asset procurement and management, empowering businesses to transform climate ambition into a clear path to net-zero. Trusted by major organizations including Deutsche Telekom, LGT, and Nasdaq, CEEZER provides the confidence needed to implement effective climate action strategies. For more information, visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://ceezer.earth">ceezer.earth</a>.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/ceezer/chief-of-staff-berlin-296659","tags":["Central Functions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1791632411},{"slug":"forward-deployed-engineer-all-genders-munich-30254","company_name":"Lio","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer (all genders)","description":"<h1>Forward Deployed Engineer (all genders)</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The Opportunity</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is fundamentally changing how enterprises operate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As AI agents become capable of executing increasingly complex workflows, enterprise software needs to integrate seamlessly with existing systems. That's where you come in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Lio, we're building <strong>THE AI workforce for procurement.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a <strong>Forward Deployed Engineer</strong>, you'll work at the intersection of Engineering, Product, and enterprise customers. You'll build integrations, solve complex technical challenges, and help turn customer requirements into scalable product capabilities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build enterprise integrations across APIs, SAP, and other business systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work directly with enterprise customers to design scalable technical solutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debug and resolve complex issues across production environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own customer-driven product features from implementation to production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build MVPs and evolve them into scalable platform capabilities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automate deployment and implementation workflows with Product and Engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn recurring customer needs into reusable product features</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Your Profile</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll thrive in this role if you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enjoy solving technical problems</strong> across APIs, integrations, and distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Take ownership.</strong> You care about building reliable, scalable solutions—not just getting things to work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Like working closely with customers</strong> and translating real-world challenges into product improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communicate clearly</strong> and enjoy collaborating across Engineering, Product, and customer teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enjoy fast-moving environments</strong> where you can learn quickly and have a direct impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Are excited about AI</strong> and the opportunity to bring it into enterprise operations.</p></li></ul><h3>What's not required</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with procurement software or SAP isn't required.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're much more interested in strong engineering fundamentals, curiosity, ownership, and your ability to solve complex technical challenges than in having the perfect CV.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Why Join Lio?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lio is back