customer projects.</p><p>You will shape the product direction, roadmap, priorities, and release process while working closely with software engineers, our Lead Architect, product teams, and business stakeholders.</p><p>The role is designed to grow into functional and people leadership responsibility for engineers working on the C++ SDK and ImFusion Suite.</p><br><span style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:18px;">Your responsibilities</span><ul><li><p>Own and continuously develop product vision, roadmap, backlog, and prioritization for our C++ SDK &amp; ImFusion Suite</p></li><li><p>Align C++ SDK and ImFusion Suite roadmap with our wider company and platform strategy </p></li><li><p>Bring together requirements from customers, internal users, product teams, engineering, and management and translate them into clear priorities.</p></li><li><p>Coordinate development activities and releases across teams and components, ensuring that individual efforts contribute to a coherent product.</p></li><li><p>Manage timelines, dependencies, risks, capacity, and technical trade-offs.</p></li><li><p>Balance short-term delivery needs with technical quality and the long-term development of the product.</p></li><li><p>Drive resource planning, support team growth, and gradually take on functional and people leadership.</p></li></ul><br><span style="font-size:18px;">Who you are</span><ul><li><p>You are a systems thinker who can understand a complex technical ecosystem, connect the individual pieces, and maintain sight of the bigger picture.</p></li><li><p>You combine genuine technical curiosity with a strong product mindset and a desire to create impact beyond implementation.</p></li><li><p>You bring clarity and structure to ambiguous situations without oversimplifying technical complexity.</p></li><li><p>You listen to different perspectives but are comfortable challenging assumptions, setting boundaries, and saying no when necessary—regardless of seniority or role.</p></li><li><p>You communicate confidently with engineers, scientists, product teams, customers, and management and build trust across these groups.</p></li><li><p>You take ownership, follow through, and proactively address risks and obstacles.</p></li><li><p>You lead through trust, constructive feedback, sound judgement, and a genuine interest in helping others grow.</p></li></ul></p><br><strong>Your profile</strong><p><ul><li><p>Several years of experience as a software engineer, giving you a solid understanding of programming and software development.</p></li><li><p>Subsequent experience owning or coordinating a technically complex software product, platform, or large-scale engineering initiative.</p></li><li><p>Experience developing roadmaps, managing requirements, setting priorities, and coordinating delivery across multiple teams and stakeholders.</p></li><li><p>Experience coordinating, mentoring, or enabling software engineers; previous formal leadership experience is a plus. </p></li><li><p>A strong understanding of APIs, software architecture, testing, technical debt, maintainability, versioning, and backwards compatibility.</p></li><li><p>Experience with capacity and resource planning, including translating roadmap needs into staffing or hiring requirements.</p></li><li><p>Hands-on experience adapting SDK requirements, architecture, and product roadmaps to advances in AI.</p></li></ul><span style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:18px;">Nice to have</span><ul><li><p>Experience with C++ development or ownership of a C++-based product or platform.</p></li><li><p>Experience with developer-facing products or SDKs.</p></li><li><p>A background in medical imaging, computer vision, or another technically complex software domain.</p></li><li><p>Ideally, you are based in Munich or the surrounding area and enjoy working regularly from our Munich office, allowing you to connect with key stakeholders in person.</p></li></ul></p><br><strong>Why us?</strong><p><ul><li><p>Shape foundational technologies used across our products and customer projects.</p></li><li><p>Work closely with experienced engineers, architects, and product teams.</p></li><li><p>Take on significant ownership and grow into functional and people leadership.</p></li><li><p>Work on challenging software at the intersection of medical imaging, computer vision, and AI.</p></li><li><p>Benefit from flexible working arrangements and a collaborative environment.</p></li></ul><p><strong>The stated salary range includes a discretionary, performance-based bonus.</strong></p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/imfusion/technical-product-owner-c-sdk-imfusion-suite-munich-107998","tags":["Technical Product Lead","Technical Product Owner","Technical Product Manager","Platform Product Manager","Engineering Lead","Software Engineering Lead","C++","SDK","Software Platform","Developer Platform","API","Software Architecture","Product Roadmap","Platform Engineering","People Leadership"],"job_types":["Experienced","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1791630567},{"slug":"research-engineer-real-time-imaging-munich-377284","company_name":"Imfusion","title":"Research Engineer – Real-Time Imaging","description":"<br><strong>Your mission</strong><p><strong><span style="font-size:18px;">Your Mission</span></strong><p>As a Research Engineer, you will work hands-on with our real-time medical imaging systems, with a particular focus on ultrasound and data streaming. You will contribute to the development, integration, and testing of solutions that connect our software with real imaging systems and hardware.</p><p>This role is ideal for someone who enjoys working close to the actual system: writing and debugging code, testing integrations directly on hardware, and solving technical challenges where software, imaging, and real-time data come together.</p><p><strong>Your Responsibilities</strong></p><ul><li><p>Develop, integrate, and test software for real-time medical imaging and ultrasound applications.</p></li><li><p>Work hands-on with ultrasound systems, tracking devices and other imaging hardware in our Munich office.</p></li><li><p>Implement and troubleshoot real-time data and image streaming solutions.</p></li><li><p>Develop and debug C++ components for system and hardware integrations.</p></li><li><p>Test software directly on imaging systems and identify and resolve integration issues.</p></li><li><p>Collaborate closely with our engineers and research scientists on new imaging solutions.</p></li><li><p>Support the transfer of new methods and prototypes into robust, working software solutions.</p></li></ul></p><br><strong>Your profile</strong><p><p><strong>Required Application Documents</strong></p><p><strong>Please upload your Bachelor’s and Master’s transcripts of records under “Certificate”. Applications without the required transcripts cannot be considered.</strong> Please submit the transcripts showing your courses and grades, not your degree certificates.</p><br><p><strong>Must-haves</strong></p><ul><li><p>Master’s degree in Computer Science, Medical Engineering, Robotics, or a related field</p></li><li style="font-weight:bold;"><p><strong>Strong hands-on programming skills, particularly in </strong><strong>C++</strong></p></li><li><p>Experience with <strong>real-time data/streaming and/or ultrasound/medical imaging</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Based in or around Munich, or willing to relocate, with regular on-site presence</strong></p></li><li><p>Comfortable testing and debugging directly on systems and hardware</p></li><li><p>Very good English skills</p></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Nice-to-haves</strong></p><ul><li><p>Hands-on experience with ultrasound or other medical imaging systems</p></li><li><p>Experience with real-time image processing or hardware integration</p></li><li><p>Python skills</p></li><li><p>Background in applied research or R&amp;D</p></li><li><p>German skills</p></li></ul><strong>Please note: This is not an entry-level position. We are looking for candidates with several years of relevant professional experience beyond internships, working student roles, or academic projects.</strong></p><br><strong>Why us?</strong><p><ul><li><p>Work on cutting-edge medical imaging technology with direct impact on real-world healthcare applications</p></li><li><p>A hands-on role combining software development, imaging systems, and hardware</p></li><li><p>The opportunity to work with ultrasound and real-time imaging technologies in a highly technical environment</p></li><li><p>Close collaboration with experienced engineers and research scientists</p></li><li><p>Plenty of ownership and room to contribute your own ideas</p></li><li><p>A growing, international team with an open and collaborative culture</p></li><li><p>Flexible working hours and a hybrid setup, combined with regular on-site work in our Munich office</p></li></ul></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/imfusion/research-engineer-real-time-imaging-munich-377284","tags":["C++","Ultrasound","Medical Imaging","Real-Time Imaging","Data Streaming","Image Processing","Hardware Integration","Software Integration","Computer Vision","Medical Engineering","Research Engineer"],"job_types":["Experienced","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1791630567},{"slug":"research-engineer-machine-learning-medical-imaging-munich-111186","company_name":"Imfusion","title":"Research Engineer – Machine Learning & Medical Imaging","description":"<br><strong>Your mission</strong><p><p>As a Research Engineer, you will develop machine learning solutions for challenging medical imaging applications and help turn research ideas into robust, working s