 can ship quality, scalable solutions; product, design, and non-technical colleagues can prototype ideas quickly using our application code and production data as a baseline; shoppers have responsive, personalised in-store experiences; and retailers and brands can configure, monitor, and analyse their campaigns across potentially billions of data points.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're agentic-first. Every engineer has access to frontier AI tooling and our own coding harness, and we expect you to use them to move faster, attempt more ambitious work, and stay fully accountable for what you ship.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a Senior Software Engineer, though Staff engineers and ambitious early-career engineers with strong platform instincts will also be considered.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Own</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product security.</strong> Own authentication across algo1, retailer and brand employees, shoppers, devices, agents, and third-party services, alongside authorisation covering RBAC and ReBAC.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Release engineering.</strong> Develop and maintain reliable, consistent automated release cycles that get changes to production safely and quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cloud environments.</strong> Manage the environments that support prototyping features across our Android and web applications alongside changes to one or more of our backend microservices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>API and event-driven architecture.</strong> Gatekeep the quality of our APIs, webhooks, and event-driven architecture in an open contributor model.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Agentic enablement.</strong> Continually improve our internal agentic harnesses (skills, context, and tooling) that allow other engineers and less technical colleagues to develop and prototype on our platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Agentic automation.</strong> Add agentic automation to all appropriate areas of the platform stack without compromising on quality.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About You</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Must Have</strong></em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Distributed systems experience.</strong> You've designed or meaningfully contributed to distributed backend systems, and understand event-driven patterns, asynchronous messaging, and the trade-offs at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>API design and evolution.</strong> You've designed APIs that other teams and clients depend on, and you understand the trade-offs between clean design, backwards compatibility, and speed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Database and schema fluency. </strong>Practical experience with relational databases (PostgreSQL or similar), including schema design, indexing, migrations, and query optimisation. Working knowledge of at least one non-relational store.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real-time data.</strong> Experience processing or analysing real-time data streams at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cloud infrastructure.</strong> Experience deploying and operating distributed services on AWS, GCP, or Azure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shipping complex, customer-facing products at pace.</strong> Evidence that you can move real software into production quickly, making pragmatic decisions without letting perfection become a blocker.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth and ambition.</strong> A career that has moved fast, where you've taken on more scope sooner than the timeline would suggest.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-native engineering.</strong> You've shipped production code with frontier AI tools (Cursor, Claude Code, or similar) and push further into agentic workflows rather than push back on them.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Nice to Have (or We Can Teach)</strong></em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Polyglot engineer.</strong> Professional software engineering experience across the stack, with your strongest work in the platform, and a portfolio of production systems you've owned end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>B2B or enterprise product experience.</strong> Background building for business or enterprise customers, where reliability, integrations, and data pipelines matter as much as the interface.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product mindset.</strong> You care about the people using what you build, and you take ownership for what your team puts in front of them, not just the part you wrote.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Containers and orchestration.</strong> Docker and Kubernetes in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Retail or personalisation.</strong> Familiarity with retail technology, commerce platforms, or customer personalisation systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Startup experience.</strong> Background working at an early-stage startup.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How We Work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a startup, so this is a high-intensity environment. The people who thrive here are curious, proactive, and love building. If you're happiest when you're creating, experimenting, and moving fast, you'll love it here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We draw our energy from being together, so this is an office-based role. I