rketing plan, and plans with managed partner accounts, as well as measurement and reporting. Proactively develop optimizations as needed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with regional marketing and direct sales teams to ensure the regional partner marketing plan complements and integrates with regional go-to-market plans</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leverage your deep understanding of various partner demand levers, to execute a range of marketing tactics that contribute significantly to pipeline and revenue goals as set in the partnership business plan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Increase engagement and preference for Optro with EMEA alliances, value-added resellers, solution providers, and other ecosystem partners via activation campaigns and marketing enablement programs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the Optro EMEA Partner Marketing leader, educate and evangelise internally to Optro and to the partner company on requirements and support needed to hit EMEA sourced pipeline and revenue targets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own regional partnership narrative development, including for joint value propositions, joint solutions, and use cases, with tailored messaging frameworks for partner sellers, Optro sellers, and partner customer personas</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the strategic business partner for EMEA Alliances Managers ensuring ongoing alignment with Sales objectives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Marketing Operations, Partner Operations, and other colleagues on campaign tracking and measurement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in joint sales and marketing pipeline reviews with partner accounts, to identify early potential issues and suggest mitigations to keep pipeline attainment on pace</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Attributes for a Successful Candidate</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">10+ years of experience in Partner Marketing, Product Marketing, Field Marketing, Demand Generation, GRC, or B2B SaaS</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant hands-on experience managing with- and through-partner demand generation campaigns with various partner types, such as advisory firms, consulting integrators, value-added resellers, distributors, and technology partners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional storytelling and communication skills, comfortable digging into technology and product details in order to craft compelling narratives for a range of buyers, including C-suite and technical decision makers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impressive portfolio of a range of high-impact content that you’ve created, both partner- and customer-facing on a range of technologies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compelling presenter, able to lead discussions and drive to results with partner and internal senior executives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record designing and executive a range of campaigns (webinars, in-person events, digital campaigns, ABM, etc) that deliverable measurable pipeline and revenue</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in high-growth B2B SaaS environments, ideally in a leadership-level IC capacity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong multi-tasker, managing multiple concurrent workstreams while ensuring strong alignment with internal and partner stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High degree of ownership, accountability, and autonomy in executing complex, deadline-driven projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of partner portals and how marketers can best leverage portals to grow partner-sourced demand at scale</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert in MDF management, including workflows and reporting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in GRC/Audit GTM roles is a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks (United Kingdom)</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launch a career at one of the fastest-growing SaaS companies in North America and EMEA!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Live your best life (LYBL)! $200/mo (USD) for anything that enhances your life</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive employee health coverage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension scheme with company contributions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation &amp; bonus program</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous annual leave of 25 days plus bank holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time off for your birthday &amp; volunteering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee resource groups</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opportunities for team and company-wide get-togethers!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>*perks may vary based on eligibility/location</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Company Values</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer obsession: It starts and ends here. Consistently ask yourself how what you’re doing creates value for our customers. It’s a mindset.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gritty resilience: Make it happen. Find a way. Move fast, stay positive, and do what it takes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive innovation: Create the future. Continuously improve what exists and invent what’s next.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Win, together: One team. No silos, no egos. Drive to be the best and support each other’s success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth mindset: 10x, not 10%. Think in orders of magnitude, not increments. Seek feedback, learn, and improve.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>Please note that background checks are required. Qualified Applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for Employment in accordance with the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers and the California Fair Chance Act. This role may have access to highly sensitive data, including employee data, customer data, company financials, and proprietary product information.</em><br /><br /><em>We love building strong partnerships, but please note that Optro cannot accept unsolicited resumes from agencies. Any submissions without a signed agreement in place will not create a fee obligation.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>#LI-Remote</strong></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/optro/sr-manager-emea-partner-marketing-london-379148","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1791636006},{"slug":"delivery-program-manager-professional-services-united-kingdom-11669","company_name":"Docker","title":"Delivery Program Manager, Professional Services","description":"<h2><strong>About Docker</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Docker has been one of the most loved brands in developer tooling, trusted by more than 20 million monthly users and over 20 billion container image pulls. From solo founders to the world's largest companies, developers rely on Docker to build, share, and run their applications across our suite of products including Docker Desktop, Docker Hub, and Docker Scout.<br /><br />We are a globally distributed, remote-first team building the tools that define how software gets built and delivered. As AI agents redefine software development, Docker is at the center of that shift, providing the sandboxed environments, verified images, and secure infrastructure that make autonomous workflows trustworthy by default.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">_______________________________________________________________________</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Docker’s Professional Services team partners with customers to turn AI and cloud-native deployments into working production outcomes. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a technically fluent Delivery Program Manager to operate delivery engagements. You will be embedded as an overlay alongside technical sales, solution architects, forward deployed engineers, and delivery partners, translating customers’ technical and business requirements into scoped service engagements and managing them through delivery.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be both builder and operator: designing repeatable service offerings where none exist today, and equally willing to roll up your sleeves to scope a detailed Statement of Work or unblock a stuck engagement. If you thrive in ambiguity, love building order from chaos, and operate with high autonomy and low ego, this role is for you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>What You'll Own</strong></h2><h2><strong>Delivery operations</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operationalize the end-to-end engagement lifecycle, from scoping and kickoff through delivery, handoff, and retrospectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Directly manage customer engagements: plan, run governance cadences, track milestones, manage risks and dependencies, and escalations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review technical assumptions in scopes and SOWs with solution architects (environments, integrations, identity, network and security constraints, customer prerequisites) so estimates and timelines hold up in delivery.</p></li><li><p style="m