></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a <strong>Talent Acquisition Specialist, Early Careers</strong>, you will play a pivotal role in shaping the next generation of AI talent at Mistral. You will design, build, and run our global early careers strategy — spanning internships, graduate hiring, and campus recruitment — positioning Mistral as a premier destination for ambitious students and recent graduates in AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a rare opportunity to build early careers programs from the ground up at one of the world's leading AI companies. You will own the full lifecycle of the intern and graduate experience: from sourcing and selecting high-potential talent through international school and university partnerships, to designing inclusive, well-structured programs that develop and convert that talent into future Mistral employees. Working from our Paris HQ, you will partner closely with hiring managers across all our departments to ensure early careers pipelines keep pace with our rapid global growth.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📌 Location:</strong> this role is located at our Paris, France HQ, with hybrid onsite collaboration.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You Will Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Design and execute strategic early careers programs</strong> with clear goals for intern and graduate pipelines, aligned with Mistral's global growth plans and talent needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner with hiring managers and the People team</strong> to define role requirements, train and scale interview panels, and align on early careers priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the end-to-end recruitment process</strong> for interns and early careers hires globally — from role definition and sourcing through offers and conversion decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build and maintain partnerships</strong> with top international schools and universities, creating sustainable, multi-year sourcing channels for high-potential candidates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build inclusive and equitable intern programs</strong> with structured learning objectives, meaningful core projects, and mentor/buddy pairing systems for every cohort</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive global campus recruitment</strong>: represent Mistral at career fairs, host on-campus events, and develop targeted employer branding strategies for student markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build scalable systems and best practices</strong> — workflows, documentation, and tools — to support rapid growth across geographies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Embody our culture</strong> as an ambassador for Mistral, on campus and internally.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proven experience:</strong> 5+ years in recruiting, preferably in tech, high-growth, or competitive environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Early careers depth:</strong> Exposure to global early careers, internships, or graduate recruitment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partnership expertise:</strong> Expertise in international school and university partnership development and global campus recruitment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Program building:</strong> Demonstrated experience building inclusive and equitable intern programs, with excellent project management skills and exceptional attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data-driven mindset:</strong> Skilled at analyzing metrics to solve problems and optimize recruitment processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global perspective:</strong> Experience with international hiring and fluent English communication; French is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stakeholder influence:</strong> Ability to advise and align senior leaders with credibility and diplomacy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on execution:</strong> Capable of balancing strategy with operational excellence, staying organized and disciplined across concurrent programs and locations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tool proficiency:</strong> Familiarity with modern ATS (e.g. Ashby), LinkedIn search, scheduling tools, and AI-driven productivity tools is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being, growth, and work-life balance. Benefits vary by country and may include healthcare coverage, parental leave, retirement plans, relocation support, wellness programs, meal and transportation allowances, and other location-specific perks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For the most up-to-date details on benefits available in your location, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://app.notion.com/p/mistralai/Benefits-at-Mistral-36e6ba59a7fe836b93dd01737fcc27ef?source=copy_link">Benefits page</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your privacy matters to us. You can learn more about how we handle your personal data in our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.mistral.ai/terms/applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mistralai/talent-acquisition-specialist-early-careers-emea-paris-134673","tags":["Human Resources"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1791628810},{"slug":"remote-devops-engineer-28165","company_name":"Swarmaero","title":"DevOps Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Swarm Aero is redefining air power, building the largest swarming UAV and the most versatile swarming aircraft network in the world. The company is moving quickly to launch the first aircraft designed specifically for swarming, as well as the Command &amp; Control software to mobilize swarms of thousands of heterogeneous autonomous assets and empower human operators to achieve superhuman results.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team has created and exited multiple startups, negotiated defense deals worth billions of dollars, and designed and built 30+ novel aircraft, with aerospace experience from Scaled Composites, Airbus, Archer Aviation, Blue Origin, and Boom Supersonic.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Swarm Aero</strong><br /> Swarm Aero builds Group 5 autonomous aircraft and Legion, our command and control platform for coordinating UAV swarms. We're backed by Founders Fund, Khosla Ventures, and Coatue, and our software is already running on real programs and real hardware. Legion is the layer operators actually touch, and it needs to ship fast, run reliably, and deploy anywhere our customers need it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong><br /> You'll be a core member of the team that builds and runs the infrastructure behind Legion. Working alongside our DevSecOps lead, you'll own day-to-day pipelines, environments, and deployments so our engineers can move quickly without breaking the things operators depend on. This is a hands-on role for someone who likes building systems more than writing tickets about them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain CI/CD pipelines that take Legion from commit to production across multiple environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage infrastructure as code for cloud and on-prem deployments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run and scale containerized services on Kubernetes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build out observability: monitoring, logging, alerting, and on-call tooling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Package and deploy Legion to customer environments, including travel to customer and test sites when deployments require it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with our DevSecOps lead to bake security and compliance requirements into the platform from the start</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help engineers across Legion ship faster by improving developer tooling and environments</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">4 to 8 years in DevOps, platform, SRE, or infrastructure engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong hands-on experience with Kubernetes, containers, and infrastructure as code (Terraform or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and owning CI/CD pipelines in a production environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid Linux and networking fundamentals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scripting in Python, Go, or Bash</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Active Secret clearance or higher strongly preferred; must be able to obtain and maintain a US security clearance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel to customer and test sites</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience deploying to air-gapped, disconnected, or edge environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in defense tech, government programs, or regulated environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting real-time or mission-critical systems</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ITAR requirement</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a U.S. citizen, lawful permanent resident of the U.S., protected individual as defined by 8 U.S.C. 1324b(a)(3), or eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Swarm Aero is an equal opportunity employer. We value diverse backgrounds and experiences and make employment decisions without regard to race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, or disability.<br /><br /><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meaningful equity in a high-growth defense technology company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive base salary commensurate with experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Medical, dental, vision, and 401k</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PTO and paid sick leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monthly wellness stipend</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Daily catered lunch (office)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct impact on a critical national security mission</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A world-class team of engineers and operators solving genuinely hard problems</p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: $140K – $185K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • $140K – $185K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/swarmaero/remote-devops-engineer-28165","tags":["Legion"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1791628805},{"slug":"lead-talent-acquisition-emea-paris-210555","company_name":"Pelico","title":"Lead Talent Acquisition EMEA","description":"<h2><strong>About Pelico</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Traditional industrial manufacturing systems were built for predictability. Supply chains no longer are. Today, real-time data is buried in legacy tools that weren't designed for constant disruption. By the time an issue surfaces, it has already snowballed, sending everyone into firefighting mode. Pelico exists to close the gap between production plans and the daily reality on the factory floor.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've built the manufacturing orchestration platform trusted by the world's most complex industrial operations : companies like Airbus, Boeing, Safran, Eaton, and Cartier. Our AI connects fragmented supply chain, production, and quality data into a single live operational picture — then puts AI agents to work anticipating disruptions, simulating recovery options, and keeping every team aligned before small problems become expensive ones.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2019 and backed by General Catalyst, 83North, and Serena, we've raised $72M and are growing fast — 300% year-over-year revenue growth, deployed in 15+ countries, and supporting factories worldwide. We're headquartered in Paris, with offices in Miami, London and Amsterdam, and we're just getting started.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a rare chance to join a company that's redefining an industry that hasn't been disrupted in decades — from the inside.</p><h2>What You’ll Do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape the talent strategy for EMEA</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build our EMEA recruiting strategy from the ground up: the processes, playbooks, and operating rhythm that let us scale hiring with quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Raise talent quality and density: define what great looks like for each role, coach hiring managers on how to spot and hire the right people, and track quality of hire.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with People leadership on a data-driven talent strategy, using funnel metrics and market insights to forecast needs and influence hiring decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create our EMEA employer brand strategy, from job sites and career page to school partnerships and events, with a great candidate experience at every step.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stay hands-on: recruit every day</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own full-cycle recruiting from kickoff through offer acceptance, with a focus on tech roles and support on select business hires.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run creative, outbound-first sourcing and build talent pipelines before needs become urgent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise hiring managers on candidate profiles, interview design, and calibration.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build a TA function powered by AI</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embed AI across sourcing, market research, candidate engagement, and recruiting operations, and keep testing new ways of working.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up the tools and ATS (Ashby) that let the team scale.</p></li></ul><h2>About You</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-powered and innovative</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You design recruiting processes where AI does the heavy lifting, and you know when to automate and when to keep the human touch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re resourceful and curious, and you bring ideas to the team rather than waiting to be asked.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>6+ years of tech recruiting experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a proven track record hiring tech profiles (engineering, data, product) through full-cycle recruiting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable as a generalist, hiring across functions and seniority levels as needs evolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re skilled at outbound sourcing and experienced with modern ATS platforms.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale-up and agile mindset</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve worked in a high-growth, fast-changing environment and love building from zero.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think like an owner, balancing speed with quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You influence leaders with sound judgment and a genuine care for candidate experience.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">International recruiting experience across multiple markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing or mentoring recruiters.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why Pelico</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building something genuinely hard and genuinely important. Here's what that comes with:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meaningful equity - you're building this with us, so you'll own a piece of it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary benchmarked to your market</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible, hybrid work model - we care about output, not face time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health, dental, and vision coverage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learning &amp; development budget - we invest in people who invest in themselves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opportunity to work with some of the world's most complex and fascinating manufacturing operations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A team that takes the work seriously without taking themselves too seriously</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Pelico is an equal opportunity employer. We're committed to building a diverse team and an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/pelico/lead-talent-acquisition-emea-paris-210555","tags":["Internal Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1791618014},{"slug":"engineering-internships-2027-paris-414780","company_name":"Nabla","title":"Engineering Internships 2027","description":"<h2><strong>About Nabla</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a team of entrepreneurs, clinicians and engineers committed to bringing back joy to the practice of medicine.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Together with a community of clinician innovators, we’ve harnessed the best of machine learning science to develop Nabla: the leading AI assistant that’s restoring the human connection at the heart of healthcare. By streamlining clinical documentation, Nabla is helping clinicians focus on what matters most - patient care. Today, over 100,000+ clinicians across 130+ healthcare organizations trust Nabla to support how they deliver care every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re at the start of an ambitious journey: Ambient listening, dictation, coding, and command capabilities are all converging into a proactive assistant that intuitively streamlines clinical and financial workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by a recent $70M Series C, we’re hiring to build the next generation of clinical AI and improve the lives of clinicians and patients everywhere.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a great time to join us!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Early Careers: Software Engineering &amp; Machine Learning </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for <strong>early-career engineers</strong> who want to learn fast, work with experienced mentors, and make a real impact from day one. You’ll join a collaborative, mission-driven team where technical curiosity and humility matter as much as skill.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Paris (Hybrid)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Start Date:</strong> 2027 (or as early as possible)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commitment:</strong>  Internship-to-hire</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we Offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real Impact from Day One:</strong> You won’t be stuck with small tasks: you’ll contribute to real features and products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning Everywhere:</strong> We believe in mentorship, pair programming, and leveling up together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lean, Ambitious Team:</strong> Be part of a fast-moving, deeply technical culture where your contributions matter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Healthcare Mission:</strong> Help doctors, nurses, and care teams spend more time with Patients</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Career Launchpad:</strong> Many interns convert to full-time, and early engineers grow quickly.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We work across multiple domains:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Apps:</strong> Web app, frontend logic, UI/UX</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Platform:</strong> Backend services, infrastructure, APIs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Core (ML):</strong> Algorithms, models, data systems</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your DNA</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Currently pursuing or recently graduated in <strong>Computer Science, Engineering, Applied Math, or a related field</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable coding in at least one: <strong>Java, Kotlin, Python, or TypeScript</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passionate about AI, data, or building meaningful product features.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious, collaborative, and excited to learn.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Humble and resilient — you ask questions, take feedback, and grow.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice-to-Haves (but not required)</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Internship or personal projects in AI, full-stack, or backend systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with React, GraphQL, or cloud infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of CI/CD, Docker, or automated testing.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’ll see us on campus at:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Télécom Paris</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Forum Trium</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ENSIMAG</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CentraleSupélec</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">École Polytechnique</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">EPFL</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Forum Organisation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meet us there and tell us what excites you.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Life at Nabla</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">When you become a part of our company, you join a team of excellence-driven, curious, and genuinely kind individuals. Together, we're committed to making clinicians' lives easier and improving healthcare experiences for everyone. We believe in a world where clinicians can focus on what they were trained to do - caring for their patients, and where no patient feels their visit was rushed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We come to work excited to leverage AI to do more for clinicians. We’re obsessed with our users’ satisfaction and we actively seek out opportunities to engage one-on-one with clinicians to understand how Nabla can better help. We consistently look for ways to improve and do not shy away from doing the work to excel. Whether it’s a feature our users asked for, or a new article for our blog, we prioritize collaboration to deliver exceptional outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We love having fun as much as we love work. Our #nablabla channel is as active as our #feature-show-off channel, we exercise during the work day at least 3 times a week (yoga, running, pilates, or HIIT, your choice!), enjoy regular off-sites to gather the team, and travel to see each other in places like NY, Paris, San Francisco, and many other vibrant cities. Oh, and we’re constantly snacking on chocolate or nuts!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this sounds like an environment you’ll thrive in, we look forward to reading your application!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our Values at Nabla</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining Nabla means being part of a team that shares a commitment to excellence, humility, growth, and inclusion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Every day is a new chance to excel</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We aim for nothing less than the best and are willing to put in the effort and dedication required to exceed standards. We learn from yesterday’s failures and do better every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stay humble</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">There’s no place for ego in our team. Our collective success is more important than individual achievements. We see humility as wisdom — keeping focus on the bigger picture.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Feedback is a gift</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We embrace feedback and foster a culture of trust and respect that helps everyone grow. We communicate openly about both achievements and challenges, and we actively involve each other in finding solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Committed to diversity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We recognize the ongoing challenge of diversity in tech. Our responsibility starts with fostering an inclusive environment where everyone feels empowered to be their authentic selves and do their best work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Diversity &amp; Inclusion</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diversity and inclusivity are fundamental values at Nabla. We embrace individuals from various backgrounds, including race, gender, educational history, sexual orientation, and beyond.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an equal opportunity employer, we actively seek out and welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds, believing that a wide range of perspectives enriches our team and enhances our ability to innovate and thrive.</p><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Avoid recruitment scams: Stay safe and informed</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">There is an active employment scam which is now using Nabla to collect personal information or financial scams. If you’re contacted by a Nabla recruiter, please ensure whomever is contacting you truly represents Nabla and is utilizing a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://nabla.com">nabla.com</a> email address. We will never ask for the exchange of any money or credit card details during the recruitment process. Nabla utilizes a hiring platform for all applications; please be aware of any suspicious email activity from people who could be pretending to be recruiters or senior professionals at Nabla. You can find more information following this <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://consumer.ftc.gov/consumer-alerts/2023/05/scammers-are-hijacking-job-ads-heres-how-spot-fakes">link</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><em>Nabla does not accept unsolicited CVs from recruiters or employment agencies in response to the Nabla Careers page or a Nabla social media post. Any unsolicited CVs, including those submitted directly to hiring managers, are deemed to be the property of Nabla.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/nabla/engineering-internships-2027-paris-414780","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris office","created_at":1791618010},{"slug":"field-sales-team-lead-lyon-french-and-english-speaking-136479","company_name":"Lightspeedhq","title":"Field Sales Team Lead, Lyon (French and English Speaking)","description":"<h2>Hi there! Thanks for stopping by 👋</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you actively looking for a new opportunity? Or just checking the market? Well… you<br />might just be in the right place!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a <strong>Team Lead, Field Sales </strong>to join our growing EMEA team in Lyon. This is an opportunity to build on the foundations of our Lyon sales team. Working closely with the Senior Manager, Outbound, you’ll coach and support the team, continue shaping our ways of working and play an important role in growing our presence in the market. You’ll join a team with ambitious growth plans and have high visibility across the organisation, with the opportunity to make a meaningful impact as the team expands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll be doing:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the Senior Manager, Outbound, to mentor, motivate and develop the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide regular coaching, training and feedback to help team members grow their sales careers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help the team consistently achieve monthly, quarterly and annual targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyse pipeline and performance metrics, identify opportunities and turn insights into action.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support outbound initiatives that improve team performance and market reach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Partnerships, Inbound, Implementation and Marketing to strengthen our customer journey and ways of working.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help grow the Lyon team’s culture, operating rhythm and local market presence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to hiring and onboarding new team members as the team grows.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you bring to the team:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a candidate who has experience with the following:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience coaching or leading a sales team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">B2B sales experience, ideally in technology, solution sales or fintech.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong understanding of sales best practices and a proven ability to close.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of meeting or exceeding sales targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A data-driven approach to decision-making and a genuine interest in performance metrics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A passion for coaching and helping others develop.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to thrive in a competitive, dynamic and target-driven environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An entrepreneurial mindset, with a bias toward action and the flexibility to adapt as priorities evolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ownership and energy to help build something new in a launch-phase environment</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Even better if you have (but not necessary):</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in the hospitality industry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with POS systems</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><h2><strong>What’s in it for you?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Come live the Lightspeed experience...</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to do your job in a truly flexible environment;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlock your potential with our growth program, paving the way for promotions and career advancement;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine career opportunities in a company that’s creating new jobs every day;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work in a team big enough for growth but lean enough to make a real impact.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>… and enjoy a range of benefits that’ll keep you happy, healthy and (not) hungry:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed share scheme (we are all owners)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health &amp; Wellness Credit- expense up to 400 EUR per year towards your gym membership, yoga classes, a new bike or whatever else you do for your health</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental Health Support through the Modern Health App- whether it is meditation, coaching or counseling you need - each employee gets access to this platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time off to volunteer and give back to your community</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transit benefit if you travel by public transport to the office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch reimbursement on the days you work from our Paris office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health insurance with attractive guarantee plan</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To all recruitment agencies: Lightspeed does not accept unsolicited agency resumes. If we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy, Lightspeed will not be responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Lightspeed is a proud equal opportunity employer and we are committed to creating an inclusive and barrier-free workplace. Lightspeed welcomes and encourages applications from people with disabilities. Accommodations are available on request for candidates taking part in all aspects of the selection process.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Where to from here?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Obviously, this has to be mutually beneficial: we want you to step into a role you love, and we want to offer you a place you’re proud to come to every day. For a glimpse into our world check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/careers/">career page here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed is building communities through commerce, and we need people from all backgrounds and lived experiences to do that. We were founded in 2005, in Montreal’s gay village and our original members were all part of the LGBTQ+ community. The ethos of our business has been about inclusion from the very beginning, and we strive to provide a workplace where everyone belongs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who we are:</strong> </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Powering the businesses that are the backbone of the global economy, Lightspeed's one-stop commerce platform helps merchants innovate to simplify, scale, and provide exceptional customer experiences. Our cloud commerce solution transforms and unifies online and physical operations, multichannel sales, expansion to new locations, global payments, financial solutions, and connection to supplier networks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Montréal, Canada in 2005, Lightspeed is dual-listed on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE: LSPD) and Toronto Stock Exchange (TSX: LSPD). With teams across North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific, the company serves retail, hospitality, and golf businesses in over 100 countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed handles your information in accordance with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="c-link" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/legal/applicant-privacy-statement/">Applicant Privacy Statement</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/lightspeedhq/field-sales-team-lead-lyon-french-and-english-speaking-136479","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lyon","created_at":1791618009},{"slug":"head-of-formal-verification-hybrid-219488","company_name":"Lubis Eda","title":"Head of Formal Verification (m/f/d)","description":"<br><strong>Your mission</strong><p><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">You own the direction of our formal verification business. Our managers keep delivery predictable. You decide what the organisation becomes.<br><br>You report to the CEO and are a member of the executive leadership team. You carry the FV consulting business as a whole — where it goes, how it performs, who leads it — and you answer for it. You will not solve verification problems, and you will rarely run a project or an account yourself. Concretely, you own:<br><br></span><ul><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;"><strong>Direction</strong>. The roadmap for FV consulting. Which capabilities, markets and problem domains we pursue, and what we decline.</li><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">Customers. You are the face of LUBIS EDA to our key accounts and at executive level. You open the doors your managers cannot, and you carry the conversations that decide a long-term relationship.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;"><strong>Organisation</strong>. Structure, standards, playbooks, talent pipelines, and the career framework in practice. You keep improving how we work, and you decide when a new technology — AI among them — changes the way we deliver.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;"><strong>Leaders</strong>. Our Verification Managers report to you. You hire them, develop them, and grow the bench behind them. This is the main measure of the role.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;"><strong>Quality</strong>. Holding the quality bar under commercial pressure. Our entire positioning depends on it.</li><li style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;"><strong>Product interface</strong>. What our engineers learn on customer projects is the best input our software roadmap gets.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Your profile</strong><p><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">You have developed leaders, not "only" engineers. You have set direction where there was no precedent, made the calls, and carried an organisation with you. You build systems that outlast your attention.</span><br><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;"><br>You need credibility in formal verification. Not to overrule your senior engineers. You need it to make the calls only you can make: is a capability gap real, is a quality standard achievable at the price we quote, does a bet on a new formal domain hold.</span><br><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;"><br><strong>YOUR EXPERIENCE</strong></span><ul><li><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">12+ years in semiconductor verification, EDA or adjacent engineering services.</span></li><li><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">5+ years in leadership, including managers reporting to you.</span></li><li><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">Fluent in formal methods and their trade-offs. Credible with a customer’s engineering leadership and on a conference stage.</span></li><li><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">You know how technical services are priced and defended on quality rather than volume.</span></li><li><span style="font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">Nice-to-have: you have scaled a technical organisation past start-up stage, where the systems had to be built.</span></li></ul></p><br><strong>Why us?</strong><p><p style="margin-bottom:7pt;"><span style="font-size:15px;font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">LUBIS is growing, and we’re looking for a Head of Formal Verification.</span></p><p style="margin-bottom:7pt;"><span style="font-size:15px;font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">This is one of those roles where you don’t just join an organisation. You help build it.</span></p><p style="margin-bottom:7pt;"><span style="font-size:15px;font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">Our formal sign-off business is growing. Our customers are getting bigger. So are our ambitions. We’re looking for someone who wants real ownership of what comes next: how we develop our people, how we deliver outstanding projects, how we work with our customers, and what world-class technical consulting at LUBIS should look like.</span></p><p style="margin-bottom:7pt;"><span style="font-size:15px;font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">You’ll work directly with our leadership team. You’ll have the freedom to shape structures and standards. You’ll build an organisation around some of the strongest formal verification expertise in the market.</span></p><p style="margin-bottom:7pt;"><span style="font-size:15px;font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">We’re not looking for someone to maintain what already exists. We’re looking for someone who gets excited about making it better, bigger and more professional.</span></p><p style="margin-bottom:7pt;"><span style="font-size:15px;font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;">If you want a leadership role with real influence, and the chance to build something you’ll be proud of, come build it with us.</span></p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/lubis-eda/head-of-formal-verification-hybrid-219488","tags":["Assertions","assertion-based","SVA","Management","Leadership"],"job_types":["Executive","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"Hybrid","created_at":1791616187},{"slug":"customer-success-manager-paris-141208","company_name":"Monday.com","title":"Customer Success Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a> is the AI work platform powering the most ambitious teams. 250,000+ customers across departments use us to bring people, workflows, and AI agents together on one flexible platform where AI doesn't just assist, it executes. We move fast, build things that matter, and foster an ownership-driven culture where you're empowered to shape how organizations work and outpace their competition.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a CSM at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a>, you will be a product master and trusted technical advisor, helping our customers build, optimise and scale their workflows. You’ll focus on the practical application of our platform, directly improving how customers work every day, including how they adopt and operationalise <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a>’s growing suite of AI capabilities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please note that this is a hybrid position with three days/week in our Paris office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll have a strong impact on our customers’ success by:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product &amp; AI Expertise</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Being a product and AI expert</strong> - master the technical aspects of our platform, including AI features, agents, and automations, to help enterprise customers solve complex business cases and define their unique setup with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operating AI-first </strong>- personally use AI tools to maximise your own efficiency every day: prepare for customer conversations using AI-generated research and account insights, automate routine tasks, and model the same AI-first working practices you help customers adopt.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Implementation &amp; Governance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Driving technical hands-on implementation</strong> - work directly with customers to set up and deploy new use cases, including AI-powered workflows, that solve real business challenges. You discover, plan and build things, not just recommend them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leading AI &amp; Workflow Enablement</strong> - lead architecture reviews to ensure scale, performance, and alignment with customer goals, and lead governance initiatives around AI and workflow orchestration.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Value &amp; Workflow Optimisation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Demonstrating value</strong> - clearly articulate the value of new and existing use cases, connecting their benefits directly to the customer’s business goals. Help customers see the ROI of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a>’s AI capabilities in terms that resonate at every level of their organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Optimising customer workflows</strong> - help customers improve their existing processes on the platform, identifying where AI automations and agents can increase efficiency, reduce manual work, drive deeper adoption and grow value. Conduct platform audits, share best practices, and document success criteria to drive performance, resiliency, and alignment to business outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic Engagement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Acting as a trusted technical advisor</strong> - engage in strategic c-suite level conversations, helping customers prioritise and unblock technical challenges throughout their lifecycle with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://monday.com">monday.com</a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Acting as the Voice of the Customer</strong> - collect and share customer feedback, including on AI feature adoption and gaps, with our product and engineering teams to help inform future development.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Retention, Growth &amp; Risk Management</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ensuring retention and growth across your book</strong> - proactively manage your portfolio to ensure long-term customer satisfaction, successful renewals and ARR growth. Building the kind of operational dependency that makes renewal conversations straightforward.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proactively addressing risks</strong> - identify and mitigate potential churn risks by ensuring customers are consistently deriving value from the platform and monitoring data signals across your portfolio.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Experience &amp; Skills</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience as a Customer Success Manager, Technical Customer Success or similar client-facing, hands-on role at a SaaS company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of implementing and configuring software solutions for clients, including hands-on platform deployment and architecture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A passion for technology and AI, with the ability to quickly learn and master new products, including hands-on experience with AI tools in your day-to-day work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to lead technical governance initiatives and platform audits, sharing best practices to drive performance, resiliency, and deeper adoption.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience engaging in strategic technical conversations with senior stakeholders (c-suite level), acting as a trusted advisor who can bridge business and technical outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills with the ability to diagnose issues, interpret data, and provide practical solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A creative, self-starter mentality with the ability to manage initiatives independently in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of how enterprise businesses operate and how they integrate software tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills, with a talent for building strong relationships across a variety of internal and external stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and executing account plans to drive adoption and ensure long-term customer success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a global team for an international company.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mondaycom/customer-success-manager-paris-141208","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1791607207},{"slug":"engagement-manager-smb-paris-125819","company_name":"Legora","title":"Engagement Manager SMB","description":"<h2>About Us</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legora is redefining how legal work gets done. Not built for lawyers, built with them. We work alongside the world’s best legal teams, who expect excellence, precision, and speed, and we hold ourselves to the same bar.<br /><br />Our AI-native workspace lets legal professionals move faster, think more clearly, and operate with sharper precision. By analysing thousands of documents in minutes and powering end-to-end workflows, we cut through complexity, teams can focus on what matters: judgment, strategy, and outcomes.<br /><br />2,100+ customers across 80+ countries trust us, including Cleary Gottlieb, Goodwin, Linklaters, White &amp; Case, Dentons, and Barclays. We’ve scaled to<strong> $200M+ in ARR</strong>, with teams across Europe, North America and APAC, and continue to expand through acquisitions including Qura, Walter AI, Graceview, Cadastral, and Wexler.<br /><br />We partner with world-class performers: including Aaron Judge and the New York Yankees, Ludvig Åberg (and his caddie), and campaigns featuring Jude Law.<br /><br />Joining Legora means three things.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>lean in: </strong>ownership over titles, outcomes over intentions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>fight for excellence:</strong> high standards, direct, ego-free feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We<strong> grow together:</strong> as a team and with our customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission before ego. Everyone contributes. No one coasts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re driven by impact, pace, and raising the bar. This is the place.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The way legal work gets done is changing, and Engagement is at the center of that transformation. We're looking for an experienced, strategic Engagement Manager to join our growing team and help a large portfolio of law firms and corporate legal teams fundamentally change the way they work with Legora.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a role for someone who has developed and executed a scaled customer motion, and who knows that transformation across a large portfolio of clients has to be designed, automated and measured. You will drive adoption, technical health and commercial outcomes of your portfolio end-to-end by leveraging systems and technology while reserving high-touch interactions for the most impactful moments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be critical as we continue to build a best-in-class adoption program at Legora, helping clients realize measurable ROI, expand successful use cases and transform the way their teams work.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Do: </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own the post-sale motion end-to-end for a large portfolio of law firms and corporate legal teams across our EMEA scaled portfolio. Specifically, you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve the scaled adoption playbook: the tech-led onboarding, enablement, and change-management motions and target outcomes for how our scale customers adopt Legora and transform the way they work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Execute against that playbook, sequencing automated touchpoints and interventions from initial rollout to firm-wide adoption and adapting as the client's needs and Legora's capabilities evolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Facilitate strategic touchpoints with your highest stakes accounts, while using one-to-many enablement to surface high-impact opportunities and guide the rest of the portfolio toward maximum value from Legora.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive sustained value through a programmatic operating cadence: templated success plans, one-to-many enablement, scaled training and digital value reviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the health of the portfolio by monitoring adoption and utilization signals in our internal systems to proactively flag and act on risks and growth opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the commercials for the scaled program end-to-end by running renewal and expansion as repeatable motions informed by exquisite portfolio hygiene, forecasting, and data utilization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Orchestrate engagement across cross-functional teams (Product, Legal Engineering, Engineering, Product Marketing, Support) to accelerate client success, maintaining end-to-end portfolio context and coordination.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate scaled customer feedback into action by collaborating closely with Product, Engineering, and Product Marketing to inform roadmap, positioning, and enablement, and to represent the voice of the scaled segment.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><p style="