/strong> Be part of the team setting the benchmark for legal AI in Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work with the Best:</strong> Collaborate with exceptional colleagues in a culture that values competence, curiosity, and ambition.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deliver Meaningful Results:</strong> Your work will directly influence how legal professionals operate—faster, clearer, and more efficiently.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Lexroom.ai"><strong>Lexroom</strong></a>, we leave buzzwords behind. Here, you’ll build something that lasts: <strong>a trusted platform, a strong reputation, a new standard for the legal world.</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lexroom</strong> is building its partnership channel and wants it to become a material driver of revenue growth. As <strong>Partnership Lead</strong>, you will own that channel in your local market (<strong>Paris</strong>): sourcing, activating and growing relationships with consulting firms and system integrators, supporting co-sell on large enterprise accounts, and contributing to early product partnerships as our API surface develops.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will turn the partnership strategy into signed agreements and partner-sourced pipeline. This is a hands-on role with high ownership and a direct line to commercial leadership.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2><strong>Your key responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner sourcing and activation:</strong> identify, qualify and onboard consulting firms, system integrators and enterprise partners, taking them from first contact to signed agreement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Relationship ownership:</strong> manage a portfolio of strategic partners day to day, running joint account planning and co-sell motions with Sales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deal execution:</strong> negotiate co-sell and revenue-share agreements within the commercial framework, working with Finance and Legal on terms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Playbook execution:</strong> apply and refine processes for partner qualification, engagement rules and co-sell, documenting what works so it can be repeated.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner enablement:</strong> deliver training, certification and co-marketing materials so partners can position and sell Lexroom independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tooling and attribution:</strong> keep partner-sourced and partner-influenced pipeline accurate in the CRM and apply the deal registration policy consistently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Performance tracking:</strong> report on KPIs (pipeline generated, ARR sourced or influenced, partners activated) and prepare quarterly business reviews with key partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-functional alignment:</strong> coordinate lead handoff with Sales, and share partner feedback with Product on integration and API opportunities.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we're looking for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partnership track record:</strong> 4+ years in business development, alliances or channel roles in B2B SaaS, including hands-on experience managing revenue-accountable relationships with system integrators, consulting firms or enterprise partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Standing and network:</strong> a strong professional network in your local market and the credibility to open doors at senior level with consulting firms, system integrators and large enterprises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deal negotiation:</strong> experience closing partner or co-sell agreements in multi-stakeholder, long-cycle sales. Familiarity with MEDDICC or Challenger Sale is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Builder mindset:</strong> comfortable working in an early-stage function where processes are still being defined, and contributing to building them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial and analytical rigour:</strong> able to track and forecast partner-sourced pipeline, and to prioritise partners and deals based on data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Languages:</strong> fluent English and native or professional fluency in the local language.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong> a legal background and/or an established network in the local legal market.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Rewarding your contribution</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation:</strong> €110,000 OTE (€70,000 base + €40,000 variable)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equity:</strong> meaningful equity on top, in line with the seniority of the role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team retreats &amp; off-sites:</strong> dedicated time to connect, collaborate and spark bold ideas</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Lexroom.ai"><strong>Lexroom</strong></a><strong>, ambition meets discipline and purpose. We’re not just building a product—we’re setting a new standard for the legal world. If you’re ready to contribute to something lasting and meaningful, we’d love to hear from you.</strong></p><hr><p>Compensation: €70K • Offers Equity • €40K Bonus</p><ul><li> • €70K • Offers Equity • €40K Bonus</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/lexroom/partnership-lead-french-market-paris-28986","tags":["Partnership"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1791574812},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-ai-native-engineering-xtm-foundation-france-449009","company_name":"Filigran","title":"Senior Software Engineer — AI-Native Engineering (XTM Foundation)","description":"<h2>🌀 The Company</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founded in 2022, Filigran is a global cybersecurity company on a mission to empower defense teams to be proactive through open-source solutions that uncover threats and drive action.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Filigran stands out in the cybersecurity ecosystem through its open-source, AI-powered and threat-informed approach to Continuous Threat Exposure Management (CTEM). Our eXtended Threat Management (XTM) platform brings together threat intelligence, exposure validation and cyber risk reduction, enabling organizations to better understand their threat landscape and take action.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At the heart of Filigran is our open-source approach. Our vision is to unite defenders into a global community to make security more open, resilient and collaborative.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Filigran continues to scale globally, we are building the organization, infrastructure and capabilities needed for our next stage of growth. How we scale matters just as much as how fast we scale: our CORE values: Cohesion, Openness, Responsibility and Equity  shape how we work together, make decisions and build for the future.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>🎯 The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a Senior Software Engineer who is genuinely, deeply convinced that AI is transforming the way software gets built, and who wants to make that transformation happen at Filigran.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an engineer first. This isn't a "we bought Copilot, please roll it out" role, and it isn't only a tooling or development role either: part of the job is building, part of it is trying things on real work, measuring them and telling teams honestly what works and what doesn't. This is a practitioner role for someone who has already lived this shift, who experiments constantly, who knows what works and what doesn't, and who can bring 60 engineers along on that journey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join the XTM Foundation team as Filigran's internal reference on AI-Native engineering. You'll propose our approach, build our practices, run experiments, and share the results so that teams can change how they work with confidence. You'll be hands-on, opinionated, and always one step ahead.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>💼 Your Responsibilities</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and own Filigran's AI-Native engineering strategy: which tools, which workflows, which practices, and how they evolve as the landscape moves fast.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run structured experiments to evaluate new AI coding tools and agents (Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Cline, MCP servers, code generation agents…), measure their real impact on velocity and quality, and translate findings into actionable recommendations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the guardrails and engineering standards that ensure AI-generated code is maintainable, tested, and consistent with our quality bar — not just fast to produce.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work directly with product engineering teams (~80 engineers) to embed AI practices into their day-to-day workflows: pair programming with AI, AI-assisted code review, test generation, documentation, and beyond.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share what you learn. Run internal talks, workshops, and demos. Be the person engineers come to when they want to understand what's possible, and what isn't. Show real results, including the failures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay permanently ahead of the curve — the AI tooling landscape moves weekly. You'll be the one tracking it, filtering the noise, and surfacing what actually matters for a team like ours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work in the XTM Foundation team to turn AI practices into shared building blocks for every product team: agent workflows in our CI pipelines (dependency updates, flaky test triage, review assistance), shared MCP servers and prompt libraries, versioned AI configuration in the repositories, and written rules on tools and data handling that apply to everyone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to Filigran's external voice on AI-Native engineering — blog posts, open-source contributions, conference talks — as the opportunity arises.</p></li></ul><h2>🤝 Who You'll Work With</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reports to: Principal Engineer of XTM Foundation team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Key collaborators: Engineers and Engineering Managers across OpenCTI, OpenAEV, and OpenGRC product teams; VP of Technology; CTO.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working model: You will split your time between XTM Foundation team work (research, experimentation, standards) and direct collaboration with product teams to embed AI practices in real engineering workflows.</p></li></ul><h2>🧬 Profile We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of software engineering experience — you are a strong engineer first. You understand what good code looks like, and that's what makes your judgment on AI credible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are genuinely AI-first in how you work. Not as a trend, not as a productivity hack. You've already transformed how you build software, you can show what you built and what you measured, and you want to help others do the same.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience deploying AI-assisted development practices within an engineering team: you've done this before, you know what resistance looks like, and you know what actually works and what doesn't.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep, hands-on familiarity with the current AI coding tooling landscape: agentic coding tools, LLM-powered code review, prompt engineering for development workflows, MCP ecosystems, and what's coming next.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong full-stack engineering background — you can evaluate AI output across the whole stack and contribute code yourself when it matters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can make a clear case, with evidence. You're a natural communicator who can discuss a trade-off with a skeptical senior engineer just as well as you can help a junior developer get started.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working in a remote-first, async culture with teams across multiple time zones; clear communicator in English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Autonomy and ownership mindset: you drive this agenda without waiting for direction, and you bring others with you rather than working alone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus: experience with open-source communities, cybersecurity domain knowledge, contributions to AI tooling projects, or public writing/speaking on AI-Native engineering.</p></li></ul><h2>🌱 <strong>Why Join Filigran? More than just a job.</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a <strong>fast-growing, global and remote-first company</strong>, and we believe the best work combines <strong>purpose, impact and innovation</strong>. You’ll work alongside talented people across the world who care about what they build, how they build it, and the impact they make on the broader cybersecurity ecosystem.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">⭐ <strong>Be part of something bigger</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe we do work that matters. Our open-source approach means that work extends beyond Filigran. You’re contributing to technology and ideas that strengthen a global community of defenders and help make cybersecurity more open and collaborative.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 <strong>Work at the edge of what’s next</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We bring together cybersecurity, open source and AI — giving you the opportunity to work with emerging technologies, experiment with new ways of working, and contribute to how they are applied in practice.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌍 <strong>Global opportunity without borders</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of a fast-growing, truly international team — collaborating across Europe, North America, APJ and beyond, with the flexibility of a remote-first environment. As we grow, you’ll have opportunities to expand your scope, take ownership, learn quickly and grow with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🧭 <strong>A culture grounded in CORE</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cohesion, Openness, Responsibility and Equity</strong> define how we work together — with openness, ownership, collaboration and respect. These are the principles that guide how we make decisions, treat people and grow together, especially when no one’s watching.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>💰 <strong>What you can expect</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive compensation + equity</strong> — everyone shares in our success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote-first flexibility</strong> — work from wherever you’re based, with flexibility built into how we operate</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>25 days PTO baseline</strong> — real time to disconnect, recharge and enjoy life outside work