pany_name":"Destinusgroup","title":"System Integration Engineer (System Engineer - Effector Development)","description":"<p>The Destinus engineering team is seeking a Systems Engineer to lead the system-level definition and technical development of our effector programmes. This role sits at the centre of the development effort – bridging operational requirements and technical execution across propulsion, structures, avionics, and seeker.</p><p>The ideal candidate brings a defence systems background and understands the full development lifecycle of a guided effector – from ConOps and requirements through subsystem design, integration, and qualification. They are technically credible across multiple domains, rigorous in their systems thinking, and effective at driving alignment across disciplinary teams.</p><p><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p>· Define and own system-level requirements for effector programmes – capturing operational needs, translating them into technical requirements, and maintaining traceability from ConOps through to subsystem specifications</p><p>· Develop and maintain ConOps and operational scenario definitions; work with the customer and programme stakeholders to ensure operational intent is correctly reflected in the system design</p><p>· Define and manage technical interfaces between subsystems (propulsion, warhead/pyrotechnics, structures, avionics, guidance, and GSE); own the ICD and IRS documentation</p><p>· Lead trade studies and make-or-buy analyses to identify the best technical and commercial solutions at system and subsystem level</p><p>· Identify and track critical components and subsystems; define mitigation strategies for technical risk and drive resolution through the engineering team</p><p>· Lead or support system design reviews (SRR, PDR, CDR) and prepare the associated technical baseline documentation</p><p>· Coordinate system integration activities across propulsion, structures, avionics, and external teams; ensure interfaces are closed and integration milestones are met</p><p>· Support verification and validation planning; define the V&amp;V approach at system level and ensure it flows down to subsystem test plans</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><strong>What You’ll Need</strong></p><p>· Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Aerospace, Systems, Mechanical, or Electrical Engineering, or a related technical field</p><p>· 5–8 years of systems engineering experience on defence or weapons system programmes – rockets, missiles, or guided weapons are a strong advantage; a background in aerospace or space launcher development is also suitable</p><p>· Proven experience defining and managing system requirements and interfaces across multi-disciplinary teams in a defence acquisition or development environment</p><p>· Hands-on experience with ConOps development, trade studies, and make-or-buy decision frameworks</p><p>· Familiarity with system design review processes (SRR, PDR, CDR) and the associated technical documentation</p><p>· Experience with V&amp;V planning and requirements traceability; exposure to relevant standards (e.g. ARP4754, DEF STAN, MIL-STD, or equivalent) is an advantage</p><p>· Solid understanding of at least one key effector subsystem domain – propulsion, structures, avionics, or guidance – with the breadth to work credibly across all of them</p><p>· Structured, rigorous, and delivery-focused – able to drive technical decisions without getting lost in analysis</p><p>· Fluent in English; German is an advantage</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/destinusgroup/system-integration-engineer-system-engineer-effector-development-zurich-495513","tags":["R&D & Engineering"],"job_types":["Mid-senior"],"location":"Zürich, Switzerland","created_at":1791620405},{"slug":"structural-dynamics-engineer-payerne-329130","company_name":