f you’re not located near one of our main hubs, we offer a monthly co-working stipend.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role<br /></strong>In healthcare, the phone is still the front door, and call volume keeps rising while the people answering it are harder to hire and keep. You'll own our North America enterprise motion across providers, payers, and life sciences, helping health organizations put agents in front of patients, members, and clinicians that are safe, fast, and fit the systems they already run. You'll have the mandate to build the playbook and the team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In this role, you will:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the enterprise healthcare function across health systems, payers, and pharma/medtech: strategy, pipeline, forecast, process, execution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define the enterprise ICP, sales methodology, and a repeatable motion for each segment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and lead a high-performing enterprise sales team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Land and expand with large health systems, health plans, and life sciences companies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work through BAAs, security review, and AI governance boards (and MLR review for pharma), starting compliance conversations in week one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with our Forward Deployed Engineers to scope integrations with the EHR, claims, and telephony systems customers already run</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help customers pick one high-volume starting point (scheduling, reminders, after-hours coverage, benefits and claims status, HCP support) and prove it before scaling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a reference network of healthcare peers that buyers can call</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead executive briefings, events, and high-stakes negotiations</p></li><li><p