on, the compliance calendar, and the controls around them need a dedicated owner.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on ownership role. The provision and returns are prepared by external providers; you manage those engagements and are accountable for the output. You'll own the quarterly and annual ASC 740 provision (deferreds, valuation allowance, uncertain tax positions, rate rec, footnote disclosures), the US federal and state compliance calendar (returns, extensions, estimated payments), and the technical work underneath it: §174 capitalization, §382 and NOL tracking.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also assist in designing, documenting, and operating controls, and write the memos that support our positions, working directly with our Big 4 advisors and external auditors alongside the Head of Tax.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Requirements</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep ASC 740 expertise at a multinational — provision, deferreds, valuation allowance, uncertain tax positions, rate reconciliation, and footnote disclosure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience owning a US federal and multistate compliance calendar (returns, extensions, estimates)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of US international provisions (NCTI/GILTI, Subpart F, FDDEI, §163(j)) and how they flow into the provision</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing Big 4 or equivalent providers and working directly with external auditors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Has built or operated SOX controls over tax, or supported a first SOX implementation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CPA</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus: pre-IPO or first-10-K experience, §174/§41 computation, §382 studies, equity compensation tax (ISOs, NSOs, RSUs), OneSource Tax Provision or similar.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Growth Potential</strong></